<%# Asking a respondent to confirm their address. Amber, not the alert pink:
    the account works and nothing is blocked — the only thing waiting on this
    is whether the organisations whose Vertos they kept may write to them.

    Its own partial rather than shared/_email_confirmation_banner, which opens
    on Current.user and so is invisible to a respondent by construction.

    The button takes no address. It mails the account you are signed in to and
    nothing else, which is what keeps it from being an oracle or a way to
    write to a stranger (PlayerEmailConfirmationsController#create). :blocked
    offers no button at all: the address is suppressed, so a link would not be
    sent, and the page says so rather than pretending. %>
<div class="you-confirm" role="status">
  <div class="you-confirm-text">
    <div class="you-confirm-title"><%= t("you.confirm_title") %></div>
    <p class="you-confirm-body">
      <%= state == :blocked ? t("you.confirm_blocked", email: player.email_address)
                            : t("you.confirm_body", email: player.email_address) %>
    </p>
  </div>
  <% if state == :pending %>
    <%= button_to t("you.confirm_resend"), player_email_confirmations_path,
          method: :post, class: "you-btn you-confirm-btn", form_class: "you-confirm-form" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
